+    /// Open a system-wide asynchronous stream of services that become newly available.
+    ///
+    /// Unlike [`Runtime::find_service`], which is scoped to a single interface `I` and a
+    /// [`FindServiceSpecifier`], this stream is not bound to one interface at the call site.
+    /// Each yielded item is an interface-independent [`ServiceDescriptor`] that identifies the
+    /// service interface and the offered instance, so the same stream can report services that
+    /// belong to different interfaces.
+    ///
+    /// # Initial results
+    /// Services that are already available when the stream is created are reported as the first
+    /// items. A stream opened while no matching service is available yields no item until the
+    /// first service becomes available; it does not terminate.
+    ///
+    /// # Items
+    /// The stream yields `Result<ServiceDescriptor>`. Items are interface-independent
+    /// descriptors, so the same stream can report services that belong to different interfaces.
+    ///
+    /// # Errors
+    /// An error is yielded inline as `Err(Error)`; it does not terminate the stream or hide later
+    /// availability, matching the error policy documented for [`Subscription::to_stream`]. The
+    /// stream itself fails to be created with [`ServiceFailedReason::NotSupported`] when the
+    /// runtime backend does not implement system-wide discovery (the provided default).
+    ///
+    /// # Lifetime
+    /// The returned stream borrows `self` for its whole lifetime; it cannot outlive the runtime
+    /// that created it.
+    ///
+    /// # Termination
+    /// The stream ends only when the caller drops it. Dropping the stream stops the underlying
+    /// backend discovery. A yielded error does not terminate the stream.
+    ///
+    /// # Default implementation
+    /// The provided default returns [`ServiceFailedReason::NotSupported`] because not every
+    /// runtime backend offers an all-services (system-wide) discovery operation. This keeps the
+    /// method additive: existing `Runtime` implementers keep compiling and the interface-scoped
+    /// discovery API ([`Runtime::find_service`]) is unaffected. A runtime overrides this method
+    /// only once its backend actually exposes such a capability.
+    fn find_all_services(&self) -> Result<Pin<Box<dyn Stream<Item = Result<ServiceDescriptor>> + Send + '_>>> {
+        Err(Error::ServiceError(ServiceFailedReason::NotSupported))
+    }
